  "number": "6.1.5",
  "title": "Sets of real numbers.",
  "body": " Sets of real numbers       Which of the sets , , , and have the integer 0 as an element?  The integer 0 can be written as a fraction, for example . Thus 0 is an element of . The integer 0 can be written as 0.0 (or just 0). Thus 0 is an element of . Since the integer 0 is not positive, 0 is not an element of . Since the integer 0 is not nonzero, 0 is not an element of .      Which of the sets , , and are subsets of the others?  Any integer can be written as a fraction, for example . Thus is an element of and so is a subset of . Any integer can also be written as a real number, for example (or just ). Thus is an element of and so is a subset of . Any rational number , where is an integer and is a nonzero integer, can be written as a decimal by dividing . We might get a terminating decimal, like , or we might get a repeating decimal, like . (It turns out we cannot get a non-repeating decimal.) Thus is an element of and so is a subset of .        "
