  "body": " Properties of Relations on a Finite Set   Consider the relation whose directed graph is drawn in .   The relation is transitive but not reflexive and not symmetric.        Is reflexive? Justify your answer.  No, while there is a loop at 1, there are no loops at 2 or 3. Thus , but and . To be reflexive, we'd need a loop at every point.      Is symmetric? Justify your answer.  No, we have single-headed arrows. For example, there is an arrow from 2 to 1 but no arrow from 1 to 2. Thus , but . To be symmetric, we'd need only double-headed arrows and loops.      Is transitive? Justify your answer.  Yes. We need to check if and , then . It turns out that there are four , pairs to check as shown in . Since for all four pairs , the relation is transitive.   Justifying that the relation drawn in is transitive       in ?             Yes       Yes       Yes       Yes          "
