  "title": "Proper Bit Strings Puzzle.",
  "body": " Proper Bit Strings Puzzle  Recall that a bit string is proper if it can be constructed from these rules in a finite number of steps (and improper otherwise):   \\textbf{~ B}:  The empty bit string is proper.    \\textbf{~ R1}:  If the bit string is proper, then the bit string is also proper.    \\textbf{~ R2}:  If the bit string is proper, then the bit string is also proper.      Explain why the bit string 1010 is proper. That means, show how to use the rules to construct this bit string.    Explain why the bit string 111010 is proper. Again, show how to use the rules to construct this bit string.    Draw a possibility tree showing all proper bit strings of length up to four. Underline the bit strings of length four in your tree.    How many proper bit strings of length four are there?    Use your tree to explain why the bit string 1101 is improper.    How many improper bit strings of length four are there? Hint: How many bit strings of length four are there (total)?    Extend to your tree from to show all proper bit strings of length up to five. Draw a box around each bit string of length five in your tree.    How many proper bit strings of length five are there? How many improper?     "
