  "body": " Explore   In this problem, we are looking for general conjectures that tell us if a bit string is proper or improper by looking at it meaning without working through the rules, drawing a tree, considering cases, or anything complicated. Your conjectures should be in the form  If a bit string is\/has \\hspace{1in} , then it is automatically proper\/improper.  Your conjectures should not be examples, they should be general rules that apply to an infinite number of bit strings.   Make a conjecture about a condition that automatically shows a bit string is proper.    Make another conjecture about a condition that automatically shows a bit string is proper.    Make a conjecture about a condition that automatically shows a bit string is improper.         Hint: One possible answer is any bit string that consists only of 0 s: 0 , 00 , 000 , etc.    Hint: Find another type of bit string that is always proper. Make sure there are infinitely many bit strings of this type    Hint: Count the number of 0 s.     "
