  "body": " Explore   Here's an alternative way to find the binary representation of the integer 100.   100 div 2 = 50 and 100 mod 2 = 0.    50 div 2 = 25 and 50 mod 2 = 0.    25 div 2 = 12 and 25 mod 2 = 1.    12 div 2 = 6 and 12 mod 2 = 0.    6 div 2 = 3 and 6 mod 2 = 0.    3 div 2 = 1 and 3 mod 2 = 1.    1 div 2 = 0 [STOP] and 1 mod 2 = 1.    The binary representation of 100 = . Note that we are reading the remainder ( mod ) from bottom to top.     Use this new process to find the binary representation of each integer. Be sure to show work.   17    45    300    1,000       Make sure to show how you are using the algorithm.        Hint:     Hint:       "
